# .gitleaksignore — audited historical findings, one fingerprint per line.
# Format: <commit>:<file>:<rule-id>:<line>. Read by the pre-push hook and by the
# secret-scan CI job, which scans full history on a pull request.
#
# An entry here means a human looked at the finding and established it is not a
# credential. It is never a way to quiet the scanner on something unexamined: if
# you cannot say in one line why the match is harmless, it does not belong here.

# The jules-dispatch test suite's synthetic API key, in the commit that
# introduced it. The fixture was shaped like a Google API key, which is exactly
# what generic-api-key is meant to catch, so the scanner was right; it has since
# been renamed to a self-describing string that matches no rule. The value never
# authenticated anything — it exists so the suite can prove the dispatcher's key
# handling refuses a bad mode, keeps the key out of argv, and keeps it out of
# child environments. This entry covers only the historical commit; the string is
# absent from the current tree.
